## Updates selector design

`updates/+page.server.ts` SSR-loads one `MonthlyUpdates` object. `lib/updates.ts` owns only `EntityUpdate`/`MonthlyUpdates` and date formatting; it has no ranking or money semantics. Rankings keeps selected category state in `+page.svelte`, derives rows from typed data, and uses `CategoryWheel` plus feature layout. `CategoryWheel` is generic over string IDs; each option provides caller-owned SVG geometry and uses native pressed buttons. `ResultRow` wraps the existing native `<li>` presentation, while `.results-list`, `.entity-text`, `.entity-name`, and `.entity-alias` come from the UI stylesheet. `RankingList` has its own ordinal and financial/bar model, so it is the wrong list for Updates.

### Smallest shape

```ts
type UpdateCategory = "members" | "companies";
const updateCategories: CategoryWheelOption<UpdateCategory>[] = /* two relevant sectors */;
const selected = $state<UpdateCategory>("members");
const rows = $derived(data.updates?.[selected] ?? []);
const title = selected === "members" ? "MPs" : "Companies";
```

In `updates/+page.svelte`, keep the existing month and title, place a `CategoryWheel` in a Rankings-like intro, and render one `SectionHeading` plus the existing results list for `rows`. Use the selector’s `onselect` to set `selected`; choose `label="Update category"`. Keep each destination, declaration count, latest registration, and the backend-provided row order exactly as they are today. A local `updateHref(category, id)` helper is optional; only add it if it removes repeated category-dependent link logic.

Reuse `CategoryWheel`, not `RankingList`. Supply two valid sector paths/options for MPs and Companies only (e.g. the existing opposing NW/SE quadrants and their labels), so no unrelated Individuals/Parties choices appear. This leaves unused quadrants; if that looks too sparse in review, a two-way segmented control would need to be an explicit design choice or a reusable wheel geometry change.

For entry motion, add a local short opacity/translate animation to the list rows and wrap the active list in `{#key selected}` so switching categories remounts it. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`. Do not add a timeout, delay data rendering, or hide the SSR-selected MPs rows; CSS motion is sufficient. Preserve `ResultRow` and the same metadata. No count or date belongs in an amount field.

### Risks and verification

Two quadrants may make the wheel composition feel unbalanced; check desktop and narrow widths, focus/pressed state, and that the accessible group announces the selected choice. Confirm initial SSR shows MPs, switching shows Companies in API order, links resolve to members/funders, the existing empty state and error state remain, reduced-motion disables row movement, and no totals/categories/dates in backend data change. Per repo UI policy: run frontend check/build and affected Playwright tests, then capture desktop screenshots for the PR.
EOF"});
